# CODEOWNERS — review routing, not a merge block.
#
# This does not by itself require review before merge (branch protection has
# to be configured separately for that). It exists so GitHub auto-requests
# the right reviewer on high-blast-radius paths, even solo — future-you (or
# a future collaborator) benefits from the routing being explicit instead of
# tribal knowledge.
#
# Add paths as the project grows real blast-radius (CI config, auth code,
# migrations, anything a bad change to would be expensive). Until then, a
# single blanket owner is enough.

